WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:00.890
You

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:00.740
Grrrr

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.820
Have you seen his vein, Foxy?

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.160
Yes, it's a variety of Nardo-status gecomandus.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.420
An uncatalogued variety.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.710
Dr. Ollison, here's the refreshment.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:47.770
Oh, that's kind of you.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:50.370
Are you too absorbed in what I have shown you?

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:52.530
Absorbed indeed, sir.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.310
No, these are wise.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.050
I thought I knew every type of plant in these mountains, but these are...

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.730
This plant we employ to cure thickness of the skin.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:02:59.820
And where does it grow?

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.920
The monks go in parties to seek all these plants.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.720
They take many days.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:06.990
Can they show me?

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.650
Now is not the time.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.890
Soon the heavy snows will come,

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.190
and the valleys will be dangerous.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:13.870
Oh.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.200
Take what is there.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:16.380
Take what you need.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.760
But these are your medicines.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.240
We have great stores of all these herbs.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.040
You can really spare them.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.520
Take what you wish now.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.240
Then you will have every species.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:27.040
Species?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:27.920
Species.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:29.980
It's a long time.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.600
since I have studied your language.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.080
The research foundation will be greatly in your debt, sir.

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.860
Mr. Fox, you do not drink your tea?

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.660
Oh, I do? Well, I mean, I will.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.670
Actually, I think I'll go and collect some jars to put these in.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.850
It will be cold.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.740
Well, really, I quite like it cold. Excuse me.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.210
Mr. Fox doesn't enjoy tea made in our fashion.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.130
I think it still seems bitter, greasy, and unpleasant, but you...

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:07.620
I've grown to enjoy it.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.190
And your wife, she also enjoys it?

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.120
Well, she's working on it.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.340
Well, she's a brave person to come here at all.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:19.180
She cannot be comfortable in those poor quarters I have provided.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.610
This is a hard, rough place built for men.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.620
You'll be very good to us, sir.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.960
Tell me, Dr. Rawlison, we are content with this land, with the people, with our...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.890
I think so. I know the Himalayas well through climbing, and now this work.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.580
You're a climber to the Great Peaks.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:43.530
I was, but I had an accident. Stupid one, but a bad one, so I gave it up.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.150
Now your wife comes with you to make sure of that?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:50.040
Helen comes with me as a colleague. We work together.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:53.240
And the other party who is coming, how long have you waited?

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.940
Six days overdue. Your wife, Dr. Ollison, she knows they are coming.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:04:59.980
Coming to help you with...

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.070
Of course, yes.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:05.670
There will be little left for them to do now that your work is almost completed.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.390
They want to see things for themselves.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:08.550
Are you permitted?

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.650
The other men, they are also sent by your foundation, or are they not?

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:16.030
They are not.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:20.580
You know something about them.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:23.300
I know they will be here tonight.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.240
I have sent guides to meet them.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:26.540
You look pleased.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.880
Of course, this is wonderful news, but I had no idea they'd be seen.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.400
They've not been seen, but they'll be here in a few hours.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:46.940
Press them in jars.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.080
The airboy's just made us a present.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.920
Pick up his collection of dried planks.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.600
That's wonderful, Foxy. Does John know?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.500
He's over there now, waiting for jars.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.180
And why there's sudden generosity from the lana?

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:57.880
I don't know.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:05:59.320
Perhaps he wants to get rid of us.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.780
So I'm ready.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.920
Sooner we get out of here, out of this infernal country

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.260
with its cold and bad smells and the superstition.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.920
Take it easy, Foxy, take it easy.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:10.260
And the misery and the ignorance

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:11.860
and this awful, awful cold.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:13.080
And the Tibetan tea.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:17.810
Say, are you busy?

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.410
Just a few diagrams to finish why.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.400
Be an angel and take these over to John for me, will you?

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:22.920
Yes.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.380
Then I can get on with the re-indexing of the new specimens.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.900
Of course. Sorry.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:36.340
I hope, sir, I can get a few more details about these,

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.300
the approximate elevation in which they can be found.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:42.340
Dr. Lawrence, what do you know about those men who are coming?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.860
Know about them? Not very much.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.040
I had a message from them suggesting we meet here.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.920
From their leader, a man called Friend.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.980
That's right, Tom Friend. You've heard of him?

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.660
He passed this way before, some months ago,

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.660
but he did not come to me as his customary.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:06:59.980
Perhaps he didn't wish to impersonate me.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.540
Now he returns.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:06.090
What is this man searching for?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.710
Before I can say that, I must have a talk to him.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:13.830
You can't say now.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:21.700
Dr. Rawlison, why do you want to help these people?

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.620
I suppose for the pursuit of knowledge.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.410
Whose knowledge? US alone?

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:29.680
All human knowledge.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:31.160
Human knowledge?

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:34.060
Is it reason enough?

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.610
I'm afraid we're taking up your time, sir.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:38.870
I don't know what's happened to Fox.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:39.950
He's not coming.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:41.950
She's your wife.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.010
She's approaching now.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:44.670
But how do you know?

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:45.990
I've been hearing.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:47.560
Is that all, sir?

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.340
Here one develops the senses, all of them.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:53.340
There's time for an awareness of many things.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.640
Have you not found it, sir?

00:07:57.940 --> 00:07:58.760
Yeah, OK.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.560
Come in. You're welcome, my dear lady.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.480
Thank you. Poxy told me to bring you.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.340
Ah, yes, thank you. We've just been presented by some very remarkable...

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:09.260
No. Poxy told me.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.900
We have not met many times, Mrs. Rollison.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:17.850
No. No, we haven't.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.110
I've talked much to your husband, but not to you.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:22.150
I'm sorry. I've had quite a lot of work to do.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:25.350
I've been concerned for your comfort, but your husband reassures me.

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:27.440
Of course. I feel we've put you to a lot of inconvenience.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.980
You are welcome to remain under my protection while your husband...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.700
is on his climbing expedition.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.010
Climbing?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:34.730
To the peaks.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:40.340
Now, unfortunately, my duties make this meeting also a short run.

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:42.690
I must leave you now.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:51.530
Climbing expedition, John.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:55.560
That was deliberate. I guess I hadn't told you.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:56.680
Well, for heaven's sake, tell me now.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.940
Perlina, I was going to explain to you before, but they may not...

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.620
It's a party led by a man named Friend. They should be here in a few hours.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:04.920
And you'd arrange to go with them?

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:09.070
Professionally, Ellen, please.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:13.380
Oh, please. There was no point in talking about it before. I haven't even told Foxy.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.140
Thanks. It's nice to be bracketed together.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.340
Oh, no, you know I didn't mean that.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.350
And what about the Botanical Foundation? Have you kept them in the dark too?

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:20.810
This has nothing to do with the Foundation.

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:24.750
Only that they've financed us here and they're waiting for our reports and we're already behind schedule.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:25.410
Yes, I know that.

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:28.790
Without being a bore about loyalty and all, don't you think we ought to get on with it?

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:33.760
Here, please, try and understand.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:37.040
I am trying, but at this time of the year,

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:39.260
with fresh snow falling to go peat-plowing just here.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.360
They may not even arrive.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:44.220
Why did we come up here, John?

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:45.140
Why?

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.130
Right up here, so far out of the way.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.800
It wasn't just to search for rare plants, was it?

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:51.860
Was it, John?

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:55.590
I'm how I knew.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.840
Kept remembering the things you wrote once.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:58.480
I said nothing.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:09:59.560
I didn't want to remind you.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:06.550
I'd hoped you'd forgotten your theories about the high valleys, about what might be there.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.100
You're getting upset about something that might be...

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.000
I'm getting to be a task of work, John. I don't want you even to do this.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.600
I can't bear it, John.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.870
Into danger, into the mountains, to look for that creature.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:52.820
what's all this in aid of oh it's just one of their regular ceremonies do you think they've

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:59.400
chosen tonight on purpose maybe hey come inside and shut the door how'd you expect me to keep

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.020
It's one of the walls out there.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:01.500
How's it coming?

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.060
I'm picking it up for an extra paw.

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:04.440
Oh, there may be even more of them.

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:07.320
Hey, you're not going to ask me to feed his porters too, are you?

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.660
They're an awful waste of food if they don't turn up.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:10.840
You know something, Foxy?

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.660
Nothing would give me more pleasure than to have to waste it.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:22.380
They're here.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:27.320
Let me know how many.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:34.100
Uh, you the head man here? You speak English?

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.380
Inzike, shigimi.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.400
Ah, where's our guide? Hey, Koussang!

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.300
He's picking up the rear.

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:41.160
Uh, you know Dr. Rolison?

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:42.690
Rolison!

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:43.390
Tom Friend?

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.400
Oh, hi. Hey, Koussang!

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:48.960
I'm here, mister.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.640
Get the stores under cover. Take care of the ponies.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.200
Ha, ha, ha! Is this it our honor?

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:55.760
I don't know.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.200
Hey, Jock, stick close. These guys will eat ya.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:11:59.620
Mr. Friend, I'm very glad to meet ya.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:11:59.960
Dr. Rolison?

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:05.660
I presume it's a great honor we've almost given you up now we ran into a little bad weather we have expected you be gone

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:11.030
This is Ed Shelley. Mr. Shelley. Hi, I'm Jock our photographer. How do you do? Oh, and this is Peter Fox my assistant

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:15.370
Well, I hope you're all hungry. There's a banquet upstairs beef stew. Lead me to it. I can eat a yak

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:20.830
I'd better warn you about Ed's table manners. Oh, and this is my wife Helen Tom Friend, Mr. Shelley and Andrew

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:24.810
Andrew McNeese. Sorry, how do you do? Well, there are four portions between three of you, sir. Come on up everybody

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:28.160
Take that you work ma'am. Come on, Jock. This is home cooking

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.120
You didn't tell me about your wife.

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.540
Don't we always work together?

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:35.000
It's hardly a trip for a woman.

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:37.080
So she stays here with Fox. I've already fixed that.

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:38.000
Fine.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:39.360
If I can't.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:40.410
If you come.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:44.500
Dr. Rollison, this is the expedition that's not going to fail.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.780
We're going to find that creature they call the Yeti.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:49.650
Oh, yes.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.810
Can we stable under there, under your living quarters?

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:53.850
That's what it was built for.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:54.980
Kusang!

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:56.090
Chakpochev!

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:57.490
Chakpochev!

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:58.800
Chakpochev!

00:12:59.340 --> 00:12:59.540
Fight!

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.540
We covered a lot of miles today. How many, Tom?

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.460
About ten.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:10.250
Ten? My street says about a hundred.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:13.400
Over all the rockiest tracks in this stinking country.

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:15.900
Thank you. Ed here objects to deprimity.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:16.720
Come on, move over.

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:17.470
Primitive?

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:20.100
I don't know what's worst about it.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:25.100
The stink of everything, or the ignorant natives, or the filthy food they eat, or what.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:25.760
You tell me.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:27.600
I find this country rather attractive.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:28.880
Attractive?

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:29.980
Oh, come on, Ed. Knock it off.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.180
Well, even what we're going to look for is abominable.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:34.820
Well, that's what they call it, isn't it? The abominable snowman?

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:36.560
It doesn't exist.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:40.040
Helen, you don't subscribe to your husband's views, Mrs. Robinson.

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:40.880
No.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.540
And about what this creature might be?

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:43.580
No, I don't.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:44.400
Neither do I.

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:47.030
Oh, skeptics riding camp, Buckerson.

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:50.970
When the whole evidence of these theories is based on a few footprints in the snow...

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:52.750
Have you ever seen these footprints, Mr. Buckerson?

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:53.350
I have not.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:55.540
I have.

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:04.420
with a climbing party two years ago.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:09.470
I found a line of fresh footprints, like human ones,

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:13.110
only bigger and far broader.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:14.970
You didn't see what made them?

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.520
I followed them for a mile or so,

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:20.390
and then they finished on a bare rock face.

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:26.240
It was just long enough to get a sense of what I might be tracking.

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.340
You're an impressionable man, Mr. McLean.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:29.970
Well, this is the sort of...

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:33.610
Also, there have been photographs, Mrs. Rolison.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:37.230
1951 Shipton expedition took pictures of similar footprints.

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:38.470
They were published in the Times.

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:39.970
They could be made by a bear.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:40.920
But they weren't.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.920
Look, in your message, you said something about having special evidence.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:45.460
So this seems to be a good time to produce it.

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:49.540
Hmm. Came into my possession a short time ago.

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:52.780
Solid silver, native craftsmanship.

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:55.530
Maybe you can read what it says around there. Translate it.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:17.060
The protection of the great bird, the powerful beings is besought by the Lama of Rongruk.

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:18.650
This monastery.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:23.010
That's right. This was stolen from here some years ago by a German explorer.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:26.730
Powerful beings, that probably means local gods.

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:29.980
Now watch. The ornamentation...

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.710
but it finally does unscrew, and you see...

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.060
Tooth.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.000
Ah. In the Middle Ages, it was a usual thing

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.130
to preserve bits of tooth and bones in the bodies of saints.

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:44.700
That's what that is, a reliquary.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:46.260
But, of course, you'd know more about that doctor.

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:52.790
Are you close, sir? Genuine?

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.460
It is. I had it sectioned and tested.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.920
It's like the canine tooth of an ape, say, a guru.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.840
It's about three times as big.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.290
Let me see.

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:09.890
Well, I've read your views, doctor, on the possible size and bone structure of these creatures.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:11.330
That would fit, wouldn't it?

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:11.930
Yes, it would.

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:13.290
But it's not a fossil.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:14.520
It's living ivory.

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:35.250
what's this a war dance these people are buddhist they don't believe in war

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:40.370
holy men doing a holy dance hey this is good job get a picture they don't allow it

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:58.640
trouble you can take my word for it well i hope you're right

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:02.650
My responsibilities. I want to find one of my porters a knife.

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:05.730
Look, friend, there isn't a bit of the harm anyone or anything.

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:08.030
Okay, just so they know it. How about some more stew?

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:08.710
Here, give me your pay.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:09.930
Just a minute. Did I hear right?

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.530
You're not taking the porters with you.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:12.470
Not beyond this point.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:13.670
You're doing this climb alone?

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:14.950
No, it's just the five of them.

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:16.410
You better tell us your plans.

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:20.060
Well, so far, no expedition's ever gotten near this thing they call a Yeti.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:20.580
You know why?

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:25.240
They'll tramp it up to the peaks with 50 or 60 porters behind them like an invading army.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.250
It's enough to scare off any living creature.

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:29.770
We don't want that, so they'll be just the five of them.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.160
What do we live on? Vitamin pills?

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.720
Ha ha! Tell him, Tom.

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:35.060
We've been up here before, Ed and I, last summer.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:35.660
Yes, I heard that.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.960
We took 50 men loaded to the limit up the North Valley,

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:41.640
salted away supplies and stores in places where they'd be safe from the snows,

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.940
rock caves and so on, all along the route.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.200
And do you think these supplies will still be there with 50 men sharing the secret?

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:48.920
They don't. We took turns.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.400
One of them marched them on while the other stayed behind and hid the...

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:52.980
the batch that they'd just unloaded.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.140
Single-handed. It was murder, but we did it.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.140
The North Valley.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:59.720
It's the steepest, the crookedest, and blocked by the worst ice folds you ever saw.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:17:59.900
Mike.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.060
The mountains and the moon.

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.300
If I were a creature that wanted to lurk away from man, that's where I'd lurk.

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:07.220
John, this is completely irresponsible. Without porters, without a guide.

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:10.360
Uh, correction, ma'am, we are taking along one local guide.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:12.200
Nima Kusang, you saw him down below.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:15.620
One guide, and how did he, he qualify for this unique position?

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.770
Because he's seen a yeti, ma'am.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:23.090
This is the time to do a dark winter.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:26.430
The heavy snow's forcing anything, it's up there down valley for food, right?

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:26.910
Yes, but...

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:28.250
It's gonna be tough going, we know that.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.960
We can use an expert climber and...

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:33.290
In a double capacity, we need you with us. What do you say, Doc?

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:35.330
Yes, John. What do you say?

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.100
I'd like to show this to someone first.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:43.480
Who's that?

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:46.860
The person who seems to be his rightful owner, the llama.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:47.660
Whenever you say.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:48.390
Now.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:50.570
Keep the food hot.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:51.410
I'll come, too.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:06.100
It's just worn, sometimes for several hours.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:07.360
Put that away, John.

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:16.490
Yes, I know this. It was taken from here many years ago.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:22.840
However you came by it, Mr. Flint, I'm grateful you return it now.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:27.990
Happy to do so, sir. You know it opens, then.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.250
The carved tooth.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:34.000
Carved?

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:38.480
It was made, though I've heard, by a monk in the far distant time.

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:42.450
It was meant to be a tooth of the god Manjouzri, the all-powerful.

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:43.030
It was made?

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:45.330
Did you think it was a real tooth?

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:46.590
We thought perhaps it was a...

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:49.720
You men of the West, you are driven by curiosity.

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:57.830
You would risk your lives in those wastes and ice and coldness to search for this.

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:01.900
He's known all the time.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.880
This animal, you only imagined to exist.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.780
You also think it doesn't exist.

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:09.020
Look, Relison, you've made no contract.

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:11.900
You're under no obligation to go up there with us tomorrow when we leave here.

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:16.640
But we're gone. And if it's humanly possible, we're gonna find that creature.

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:20.020
I'll come.

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:23.270
Don't worry, he'll be all right. We'll look after him.

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:23.810
You'll be just...

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:29.870
If you have my part in myself, I'd like to thank you for your hospitality.

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:34.250
Small return, Mr. Friend, for this.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:42.900
Okay, emergency rations packed and checked. What's next?

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:45.300
Snow crampons. Crampons? Cousin's getting them.

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:47.470
Cousin! Chuck Poche!

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:50.960
Here, watch these guys. They got a greedy look.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.680
Oh, I don't think they... Just watch them, that's all.

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:57.950
Come on, give us that. Hey, Cousin, did you talk to the other porters?

00:20:58.030 --> 00:20:59.970
Yes, mister, they want pay now. They'll get paid.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.580
When we get back, how come we only got three packed?

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:04.960
Rolison says he's got his own gear.

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:09.740
Goodbye, Foxy. Look after her.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:10.320
I will.

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:10.880
See you soon.

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:14.590
Well, I'd better get back to those reports.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:19.230
See, he disapproves.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.680
You'd better bracket us together again.

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:22.740
No, I thought we said...

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:25.760
I know, John, but it's those men, Friend and Shelley.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:27.240
I don't trust them, I don't like them...

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:28.760
You're just grabbing at straws now.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:29.980
No, no, I mean...

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:33.920
Listen, friend talks too much, agreed, and Shelly could use a few manners.

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:35.980
All right, I snore. They'll be the ones to suffer.

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:37.500
Don't joke about it, John.

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.460
Helen, darling, look, you do understand.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:44.110
I've written and talked enough about this thing.

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:45.590
Now I've got a chance to put it all to the test.

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:47.030
I've just got to take it, haven't I?

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:49.890
Come on, now. Give me a hand with this.

00:22:00.990 --> 00:22:03.540
John, for the last time I'm asking you, don't go.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:04.640
Look, darling.

00:22:05.080 --> 00:22:06.900
You won't come back. I know it. I'll never see you again.

00:22:12.300 --> 00:22:13.770
Come on, we gotta move.

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:18.360
Careful, my darling. Be careful.

00:22:18.640 --> 00:22:20.460
I can look after myself, you know that.

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:23.720
Listen!

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:38.180
Who say?

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:39.000
Push eye!

00:23:14.650 --> 00:23:17.050
Wait a minute. We got to keep this pace up.

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:19.290
We got to make that hut before nightfall.

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:21.730
Yeah, we went an easier way last time, over those ridges.

00:23:21.890 --> 00:23:23.270
This time of year, they're all snowed up.

00:23:23.390 --> 00:23:25.870
Yeah, well, look at those characters. They seem to be doing all right.

00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:27.840
Yeah, well, they're not going where we're going.

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:29.280
You all right, Doc?

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.140
Well, let's keep moving, nice and steady.

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:33.860
Yeah, get a rhythm. Maybe we ought to sing or something.

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:34.840
Yeah, you do that.

00:23:35.020 --> 00:23:35.200
Huh?

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:35.640
Sing!

00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:39.540
John Brown's body.

00:23:40.200 --> 00:23:41.480
Well, come on, sing!

00:23:42.390 --> 00:23:46.330
John Brown's body lies a-molding in the grave.

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:49.850
John Brown's body lies a-molding in the grave.

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:05.000
A tavern in the town, in the town.

00:24:05.300 --> 00:24:06.380
Save your breath, will you?

00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:07.990
We're making good time, ain't we?

00:24:08.350 --> 00:24:10.630
Yeah, but where do we really start to climb?

00:24:17.110 --> 00:24:18.810
Come on, Ed, we've got to keep this pace up.

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:20.450
Why pick on me? What about Leadfoot?

00:24:20.970 --> 00:24:22.730
Him I can do without. You I need.

00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:24.970
Let's stop bickering. We've got less than two hours to sunset.

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:26.630
We've got to be on a safe campsite by then.

00:24:26.710 --> 00:24:27.950
When we get to Hutt, we'll be all right.

00:24:28.130 --> 00:24:29.410
Where exactly is this Hutt?

00:24:30.730 --> 00:24:31.490
Over that ridge?

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:33.560
There's a lot of rough weather coming up.

00:24:33.700 --> 00:24:35.100
We never make it in the time unless...

00:24:35.100 --> 00:24:35.380
Ah.

00:24:35.620 --> 00:24:36.440
There is a shortcut.

00:24:36.780 --> 00:24:37.020
Where?

00:24:37.220 --> 00:24:38.520
Across the car on that side.

00:24:39.100 --> 00:24:40.220
It looks awful steep.

00:24:40.830 --> 00:24:41.810
Well, let's give it a try.

00:24:42.730 --> 00:24:44.310
You're the prize climber in this party, Doc.

00:24:44.450 --> 00:24:45.370
Why don't you take over?

00:24:45.450 --> 00:24:46.530
All right, everybody rope up.

00:24:46.650 --> 00:24:47.110
We need it from here on.

00:24:47.130 --> 00:24:47.430
Who's that?

00:24:47.570 --> 00:24:47.790
Rope?

00:24:47.910 --> 00:24:49.130
It'll be a short, sharp climb.

00:24:49.370 --> 00:24:50.190
So long as it's short.

00:24:50.270 --> 00:24:51.470
Fairly short, as these things go.

00:24:51.590 --> 00:24:52.990
You'd better take the middle position for safety.

00:24:53.110 --> 00:24:54.090
I like safety too, Doc.

00:24:54.270 --> 00:24:56.050
We'll be all right if we keep our minds on what we're doing.

00:24:56.230 --> 00:24:57.770
Well, let's get roped up and get on with it.

00:24:58.790 --> 00:24:59.430
Choc-pouché.

00:25:00.090 --> 00:25:00.770
You first.

00:25:01.540 --> 00:25:02.300
Let's get going, Doc.

00:25:02.460 --> 00:25:03.160
Come on, Ed.

00:25:03.720 --> 00:25:04.720
Okay, we're coming.

00:25:04.960 --> 00:25:05.380
Joe!

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:15.280
Oh crap!

00:25:16.230 --> 00:25:16.510
Oh my God!

00:25:22.780 --> 00:25:25.180
Had nothing, just some small stuff came down.

00:25:25.340 --> 00:25:27.610
For a minute there I thought we had an avalanche starting.

00:25:27.790 --> 00:25:29.550
And it might have been, it was his fault yelling like that.

00:25:29.570 --> 00:25:29.730
Yeah.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.140
No, he isn't.

00:25:31.532 --> 00:25:33.532
A sharp sound, sudden rubation, that's all it takes.

00:25:33.532 --> 00:25:35.032
So let's have no more shouting unless it's vital.

00:25:35.032 --> 00:25:36.032
Right, you got that, Eddie?

00:25:36.032 --> 00:25:37.032
Okay, okay.

00:25:37.032 --> 00:25:38.032
Come on, let's go.

00:27:30.956 --> 00:27:31.456
There it is.

00:27:32.364 --> 00:27:32.864
Cut!

00:27:43.660 --> 00:27:46.460
There's nothing else in here, Tom. It was all sealed in these containers.

00:27:46.636 --> 00:27:47.416
Fill the hole up again.

00:27:47.556 --> 00:27:48.176
Fill it up?

00:27:48.296 --> 00:27:51.336
The accords will be up this spring and think the earth devils have been burrowing.

00:27:51.556 --> 00:27:52.816
Go ahead and fill it up.

00:27:52.876 --> 00:27:54.876
You want to scare these poor ignorant natives to death?

00:27:55.276 --> 00:27:56.316
You're civilized, ma'am.

00:27:56.376 --> 00:27:57.016
All right, tomorrow.

00:27:57.136 --> 00:27:58.796
If this is the way you plan the rest of the trip,

00:27:58.876 --> 00:27:59.796
the cash is under the floor.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:01.980
I wouldn't get a meal like this out of an emergency pack.

00:28:02.270 --> 00:28:02.950
Who's for more?

00:28:03.150 --> 00:28:03.790
Not for me, thanks.

00:28:04.590 --> 00:28:07.690
I thought altitude was supposed to make you hungry, Cousin.

00:28:07.930 --> 00:28:09.810
Now, do you talk about this as if it was a joke?

00:28:09.930 --> 00:28:12.070
Have you seriously considered what might happen if...

00:28:12.070 --> 00:28:15.070
Look, Doc, I've been running into people all my life who cried off

00:28:15.070 --> 00:28:18.170
because what might happen if I went ahead and did it?

00:28:19.140 --> 00:28:20.120
And now for some fact.

00:28:21.040 --> 00:28:23.000
I got some real supplies cashed up ahead.

00:28:23.140 --> 00:28:24.920
This was just a snack on the way up.

00:28:25.020 --> 00:28:27.240
And what else have you got cashed away up there besides food?

00:28:27.790 --> 00:28:29.980
Everything we need from tents to...

00:28:30.030 --> 00:28:37.160
Fuel, look, 18,000 feet will stop and make our first camp and search at the foot of the icefall.

00:28:37.660 --> 00:28:41.450
20,000 feet, the same procedure, and again at 22,000 feet.

00:28:42.040 --> 00:28:43.860
And we've got oxygen if we have to go higher.

00:28:44.320 --> 00:28:47.590
We've got everything we need to get up above this creature.

00:28:47.940 --> 00:28:50.120
Search it out in its own ground and track it down.

00:28:51.600 --> 00:28:52.820
How about some more of your contribution?

00:28:53.180 --> 00:28:53.740
What's that to ask?

00:28:53.950 --> 00:28:54.750
Expert advice.

00:28:56.780 --> 00:28:58.630
Let's know the nature of the enemy.

00:28:58.940 --> 00:28:59.760
What's it live on?

00:29:00.090 --> 00:29:02.620
Or smaller animals, hares, mice, voles.

00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:03.400
But we've seen them.

00:29:03.440 --> 00:29:04.820
Oh, you don't see them, but he's right.

00:29:04.960 --> 00:29:05.240
They're there.

00:29:05.400 --> 00:29:06.200
Can never say that.

00:29:06.340 --> 00:29:06.960
Oh, needn't be.

00:29:07.470 --> 00:29:08.990
Better root some plants out of the snow, too.

00:29:09.090 --> 00:29:10.990
It's probably fairly adaptable, like man.

00:29:12.870 --> 00:29:13.250
Not sure.

00:29:13.880 --> 00:29:16.420
Suggesting roughly is that this might be some kind of a missing link.

00:29:16.770 --> 00:29:17.670
That's a bit too rough.

00:29:17.770 --> 00:29:19.270
Say parallel development, my will you?

00:29:20.170 --> 00:29:21.270
Parallel with mankind.

00:29:24.730 --> 00:29:26.230
We're not very far north of India.

00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:29.780
Now, some millions of years ago, that was the breeding ground of huge...

00:29:30.160 --> 00:29:34.120
Ape-like animals, primitive anthropoids, their fossil bones are dug up from time to time.

00:29:34.360 --> 00:29:39.320
Now, the latest evolutionary theory is that their descendants branched off in two directions.

00:29:39.750 --> 00:29:44.550
One to become the great apes, chimpanzees, orangutans, and so on, and the other, man.

00:29:45.190 --> 00:29:48.170
Yeah, Darwin's theory all tidied up, so?

00:29:48.370 --> 00:29:52.440
Well, suppose, suppose there were a third line of descent.

00:29:53.310 --> 00:29:56.090
Anthropoid X is different from man as the apes are.

00:29:56.170 --> 00:29:56.570
Probably.

00:29:57.780 --> 00:29:59.700
Calls for some very fancy guesswork.

00:30:00.120 --> 00:30:01.220
What would have happened to them?

00:30:01.680 --> 00:30:04.220
Gradual extinction through changing conditions, attacks of enemies.

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:05.820
Might include both apes and men.

00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:06.560
Most likely did.

00:30:06.980 --> 00:30:08.480
Until only our remnants survived,

00:30:08.940 --> 00:30:11.660
adapting themselves to living where nothing else would, in these mountains.

00:30:12.160 --> 00:30:14.180
The highest in the world and above the snow line.

00:30:14.340 --> 00:30:15.480
There's no proof of all this.

00:30:15.600 --> 00:30:19.140
Not yet, but a hundred years ago, there was no proof that primitive man had ever existed either.

00:30:19.320 --> 00:30:21.760
Look, how do you see it? I mean, it walks on two legs.

00:30:21.820 --> 00:30:23.280
There's no doubt about that. The tracks prove it.

00:30:23.560 --> 00:30:26.020
They show a foot 13 inches long and very wide indeed.

00:30:26.530 --> 00:30:29.960
The stride of a six-foot man, yet his date would be far more...

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.800
and very short in proportion to its height.

00:30:31.920 --> 00:30:33.340
Now, you see what that implies?

00:30:34.140 --> 00:30:34.760
It's big.

00:30:35.140 --> 00:30:36.460
Perhaps seven or eight feet high.

00:30:37.610 --> 00:30:38.230
What do you think, Ed?

00:30:39.080 --> 00:30:39.900
Well, can try.

00:30:40.850 --> 00:30:42.310
Go on, drag it out. Good a time, is it?

00:30:42.550 --> 00:30:43.250
I'm not with you.

00:30:44.420 --> 00:30:46.740
Well, we might as well let you in on our little secret, Doc.

00:30:47.400 --> 00:30:50.200
The fact of the matter is that Ed here is an expert trapper.

00:30:50.360 --> 00:30:52.340
Yeah, everything from foxies to grizzlies.

00:30:53.570 --> 00:30:56.730
Now, there's a tungsten still, Ned.

00:30:56.890 --> 00:30:57.830
It's just a little sample.

00:30:58.340 --> 00:30:59.080
You think it'll hold it?

00:31:00.280 --> 00:31:01.440
We have other things up there.

00:31:01.600 --> 00:31:02.880
What things? More guns.

00:31:04.130 --> 00:31:06.190
So that's what this is. A hunting party.

00:31:06.540 --> 00:31:09.120
What did you expect us to do? Look at it through a telescope?

00:31:09.360 --> 00:31:10.960
Have, have Jock here take a picture?

00:31:10.960 --> 00:31:12.660
You represented this as a bona fide investigation.

00:31:13.020 --> 00:31:15.120
It is bona fide. I want one alive, and so do you.

00:31:15.120 --> 00:31:16.260
And what are your interests? Commercial?

00:31:16.520 --> 00:31:17.460
Well, if they are, they're honest.

00:31:17.560 --> 00:31:18.660
Then why all the secrecy?

00:31:18.740 --> 00:31:19.920
For a thing just like this.

00:31:21.130 --> 00:31:23.090
Outraged indignation. I wanted to be well under way.

00:31:23.350 --> 00:31:23.710
Listen. Listen.

00:31:24.240 --> 00:31:24.600
What is it?

00:31:24.700 --> 00:31:28.380
It is certain I heard something, but you were talking so loudly.

00:31:29.550 --> 00:31:29.830
Outside?

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:30.380
What?

00:31:30.520 --> 00:31:32.690
A sort of cry.

00:31:33.670 --> 00:31:45.180
You hear anything?

00:31:45.540 --> 00:31:46.440
Keep the voices down.

00:31:47.480 --> 00:31:48.540
Snow-harmock.

00:31:48.620 --> 00:31:48.940
You sure?

00:31:49.290 --> 00:31:49.650
Quiet.

00:31:52.520 --> 00:31:52.900
It's nothing.

00:31:53.190 --> 00:31:54.290
But I'm sure I heard something.

00:31:55.990 --> 00:31:56.970
Any of the rest of you hear anything?

00:31:57.420 --> 00:31:58.240
No, no, no.

00:32:00.280 --> 00:32:00.940
It's false alarm.

00:32:02.360 --> 00:32:03.380
Jock, you need some sleep.

00:32:04.090 --> 00:32:04.670
We all do.

00:32:05.120 --> 00:32:05.540
Come on.

00:32:10.660 --> 00:32:12.560
Sorry I broke out at you like that just now.

00:32:13.450 --> 00:32:15.730
Put all of it on edge, leave it on the altitude.

00:32:16.400 --> 00:32:17.720
Yeah, well, I think I ought to explain.

00:32:18.740 --> 00:32:20.940
Frankly, I am, and this is a commercial venture,

00:32:21.100 --> 00:32:24.240
but I don't think that cheapens my motives in any way.

00:32:24.500 --> 00:32:25.500
What's at the end of the line?

00:32:25.680 --> 00:32:26.080
A circus?

00:32:26.260 --> 00:32:26.640
A zoo?

00:32:26.940 --> 00:32:27.660
No, me too.

00:32:30.220 --> 00:32:30.500
Thanks.

00:32:30.810 --> 00:32:34.620
Look, I'm not exactly a golden character, Doc.

00:32:35.800 --> 00:32:38.180
After the war, I did a little smuggling around the coasts of Europe.

00:32:39.030 --> 00:32:40.750
Odd gun for the angry little countries.

00:32:41.770 --> 00:32:44.620
I lived on two of the basic drives of humanity.

00:32:45.680 --> 00:32:46.420
Fear and hunger.

00:32:46.580 --> 00:32:48.900
When it began to dry upon me, I looked around for another one.

00:32:49.780 --> 00:32:51.970
On curiosity. Human curiosity.

00:32:52.900 --> 00:32:54.100
Funny thing, you ever think about it?

00:32:54.220 --> 00:32:55.620
Oh, I suppose I've suffered under it?

00:32:55.850 --> 00:32:58.390
Look, the world is full of receptive, inquisitive people.

00:32:58.570 --> 00:32:59.710
People who are informed.

00:33:02.160 --> 00:33:05.260
radio, television, films, these things have gone to the very homes of the people

00:33:05.260 --> 00:33:08.610
that stirred up a healthy curiosity about the earth that they live on.

00:33:08.980 --> 00:33:10.260
These are the people I work for.

00:33:11.540 --> 00:33:13.850
If I can, I'm gonna bring them one of these creatures.

00:33:14.110 --> 00:33:16.060
They can learn and profit from it.

00:33:16.720 --> 00:33:18.040
You really believe all that?

00:33:19.500 --> 00:33:20.260
Sure I do, Doc.

00:33:20.700 --> 00:33:25.000
They give the world a whole new concept, a new slant on humanity.

00:33:25.350 --> 00:33:26.890
Help us to know and understand ourselves.

00:33:27.490 --> 00:33:29.250
Don't you think that's important?

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:38.760
with this creature showed on television and so on those are the means i'll use them look don't you

00:33:38.760 --> 00:33:44.440
understand dr rollison writing learned little books in the corner isn't enough anymore it's

00:33:44.460 --> 00:33:51.360
a new age of awareness it's a big age to measure up to it i better get some sleep you've got an

00:33:51.360 --> 00:33:51.900
Early start.

00:33:52.480 --> 00:33:54.120
Yeah, well, you think about it.

00:34:22.400 --> 00:34:23.020
I'm done with it!

00:34:23.280 --> 00:34:24.200
I'm done with it!

00:34:24.200 --> 00:34:24.460
I'm done with it!

00:34:32.750 --> 00:34:36.110
All right, you'll get paid when Sive comes back.

00:34:36.490 --> 00:34:37.510
Now, shut up!

00:34:38.010 --> 00:34:39.770
Now, go on. Go on.

00:34:42.300 --> 00:34:44.200
It's all right. It's only friends' porters.

00:34:44.480 --> 00:34:45.740
Apparently, they haven't been paid.

00:34:46.590 --> 00:34:47.430
Give you a bit of a shot.

00:34:47.650 --> 00:34:49.210
Now, you sit down there.

00:34:49.540 --> 00:34:50.380
Have a spot of this.

00:34:50.540 --> 00:34:51.460
It'll make for you much better.

00:34:52.420 --> 00:34:54.980
Why do you suppose he didn't pay them, Foxy?

00:34:55.420 --> 00:34:57.860
Oh, just to make sure they're here when he comes back.

00:34:58.900 --> 00:34:59.980
Customary and reasonable.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:01.940
Then why do they suddenly behave like that?

00:35:02.190 --> 00:35:03.110
Well, you know what they are.

00:35:03.150 --> 00:35:03.990
They've got nothing to do.

00:35:04.090 --> 00:35:07.310
They stand about and chatter and argue and work themselves up, drink this.

00:35:07.330 --> 00:35:07.810
Was that all?

00:35:08.090 --> 00:35:08.470
What do you mean?

00:35:08.850 --> 00:35:10.150
It's as if they knew something.

00:35:10.560 --> 00:35:12.340
As if they knew friend wasn't coming back.

00:35:12.360 --> 00:35:12.620
No, I haven't.

00:35:12.620 --> 00:35:15.540
Or John or any of the potter. They're going to die and everybody in this place knows it.

00:35:15.560 --> 00:35:17.480
Now, stop it, then. You're talking raving nonsense.

00:35:18.000 --> 00:35:18.980
Now, come on, drink this.

00:35:23.120 --> 00:35:24.620
You didn't sleep last night, did you?

00:35:25.500 --> 00:35:27.740
Well, make sure you do in future. You take some tablets.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.760
I lay the whole night just thinking. I never felt so lonely.

00:35:34.670 --> 00:35:37.970
Now and then I heard a gong across the courtyard and the wind.

00:35:39.550 --> 00:35:42.570
Foxy. You know these things these people believe in?

00:35:43.250 --> 00:35:44.750
Clairvoyance, thought transference.

00:35:44.980 --> 00:35:45.900
Sham magic.

00:35:46.680 --> 00:35:47.440
Is it sham?

00:35:48.080 --> 00:35:50.460
Helen, this country's rotten with superstition.

00:35:50.880 --> 00:35:53.820
It's only dangerous because we're surrounded by people who think it's real.

00:35:54.380 --> 00:35:56.460
Well, we can slide into thinking it's real, too.

00:35:56.970 --> 00:35:59.060
Now, come on, drink that up. Feel much better.

00:36:00.120 --> 00:36:02.740
To make sure you're not pursued by the lads of the village again.

00:36:03.080 --> 00:36:04.500
I think I'll go and have a word with the llama.

00:36:04.680 --> 00:36:05.340
It's a good idea.

00:36:05.960 --> 00:36:07.160
You'll stay right there.

00:36:08.170 --> 00:36:09.950
If you should feel like another nip of that,

00:36:10.460 --> 00:36:11.820
nobody's going to call you a tipler.

00:37:46.890 --> 00:37:48.430
They're practically out of sight now.

00:37:48.840 --> 00:37:49.940
Yes, going well, too.

00:37:51.320 --> 00:37:53.060
How much longer will this take?

00:37:53.240 --> 00:37:54.180
I found what I wanted.

00:37:54.710 --> 00:37:57.840
Evidence of a possible food supply, type of moss.

00:37:58.620 --> 00:37:59.360
Highly nutritious.

00:38:00.890 --> 00:38:02.660
You mean, it's food.

00:38:03.300 --> 00:38:03.960
It might be.

00:38:06.290 --> 00:38:07.070
Look, let's go on.

00:38:07.390 --> 00:38:09.690
I don't want that swine to get too far out of sight.

00:38:10.060 --> 00:38:10.860
You don't trust him?

00:38:11.120 --> 00:38:12.750
Tom Friend, no more than you do.

00:38:12.890 --> 00:38:14.150
You're not a very good climber, either.

00:38:14.230 --> 00:38:15.510
Why did you come on this trip like me?

00:38:16.270 --> 00:38:16.910
I had to.

00:38:18.310 --> 00:38:18.970
You had to.

00:38:19.190 --> 00:38:22.050
Ever since that time, two years ago,

00:38:23.110 --> 00:38:25.710
I felt that this is what I must do.

00:38:25.870 --> 00:38:27.790
It's a sort of obsession.

00:38:29.420 --> 00:38:29.960
Perhaps a...

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:31.940
The psychologist could explain it. I don't know.

00:38:32.960 --> 00:38:34.880
All I know is that I've got to find the thing.

00:38:35.100 --> 00:38:36.740
Getting into it before whetted your appetite.

00:38:37.040 --> 00:38:37.980
It's all that matters.

00:38:38.610 --> 00:38:44.480
I applied to join all sorts of climbing expeditions,

00:38:45.320 --> 00:38:46.240
hoping I'd be able...

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:49.740
But I was turned down every time.

00:38:50.430 --> 00:38:52.010
Then you heard about the Tom Friend expedition.

00:38:52.510 --> 00:38:53.670
He wasn't so particular.

00:38:55.040 --> 00:38:56.580
I paid him to let me come.

00:38:57.670 --> 00:38:58.410
You paid him.

00:38:59.690 --> 00:38:59.970
I...

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.700
I can be useful. I'm good with a camera.

00:39:01.990 --> 00:39:04.370
But not so good with an ice axe. A man like you can be dangerous.

00:39:04.980 --> 00:39:06.280
No, I'll try not to be.

00:39:07.890 --> 00:39:08.350
Come on.

00:40:30.920 --> 00:40:37.830
I said it pitched camp at the icefall.

00:40:38.120 --> 00:40:39.100
They're right in the middle of it.

00:40:39.220 --> 00:40:41.230
Now, they can't be far away.

00:40:43.420 --> 00:40:43.760
Hello?

00:40:46.380 --> 00:40:46.840
Wait a minute.

00:40:49.050 --> 00:40:50.010
I thought I heard something.

00:40:52.560 --> 00:40:53.100
Why is it?

00:40:58.740 --> 00:40:59.140
Are you in the...

00:41:02.520 --> 00:41:02.920
Help!

00:41:20.860 --> 00:41:23.260
It can't make me!

00:41:23.610 --> 00:41:24.670
It fastens, look!

00:41:30.090 --> 00:41:33.840
Hell, that's that! It's valuable!

00:41:35.600 --> 00:41:37.600
Here, here, let me do that.

00:41:37.780 --> 00:41:38.620
Did you set this?

00:41:38.840 --> 00:41:40.230
What do you think?

00:41:40.600 --> 00:41:41.580
Without warning us?

00:41:42.370 --> 00:41:43.930
You want to put a flag on it or something?

00:41:45.060 --> 00:41:46.260
Did I know you was coming this way?

00:41:46.360 --> 00:41:47.120
Get him free!

00:41:49.400 --> 00:41:50.560
Okay, get your foot out!

00:41:52.630 --> 00:41:54.250
Oh, he's not a bad.

00:41:55.210 --> 00:41:57.050
This is my improvement on a bear trap.

00:41:57.410 --> 00:41:59.070
It grips but doesn't tear.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.100
Didn't even bite through the boot.

00:42:01.220 --> 00:42:03.000
All the idiotic, maniac ideas.

00:42:03.880 --> 00:42:05.840
What have you heard you achieve setting these things at random?

00:42:05.840 --> 00:42:06.620
We've achieved it.

00:42:07.420 --> 00:42:08.980
Before you blow your top, Doc, listen.

00:42:09.720 --> 00:42:10.580
It worked.

00:42:10.940 --> 00:42:11.320
Works?

00:42:11.620 --> 00:42:13.140
We can't one of those things.

00:42:16.180 --> 00:42:17.340
You don't believe me?

00:42:17.980 --> 00:42:18.900
Well, come and look.

00:42:22.070 --> 00:42:22.690
Watch out.

00:42:23.220 --> 00:42:24.260
It's ice up here.

00:42:25.960 --> 00:42:26.640
Give a hand.

00:42:26.780 --> 00:42:26.980
Here.

00:42:27.670 --> 00:42:27.810
Here.

00:42:27.970 --> 00:42:28.090
Here.

00:42:28.460 --> 00:42:28.720
Right.

00:42:30.920 --> 00:42:32.180
We found these little tracks, see?

00:42:32.520 --> 00:42:34.880
So I set traps on the chance that whatever made them might come back.

00:42:34.940 --> 00:42:35.520
Little tracks?

00:42:35.840 --> 00:42:37.020
Yeah, you wait and see.

00:42:40.100 --> 00:42:41.360
Hey, Tom, they're here!

00:42:41.800 --> 00:42:42.060
Good.

00:42:42.920 --> 00:42:44.690
Cousin, hold it tighter.

00:42:45.780 --> 00:42:46.560
Throw me that top one.

00:42:49.200 --> 00:42:54.440
That's where they made it, huh?

00:42:58.340 --> 00:42:58.860
There it is.

00:43:00.830 --> 00:43:01.850
Not very big, isn't it, Doc?

00:43:02.880 --> 00:43:04.040
Up more than four feet high.

00:43:04.840 --> 00:43:05.920
But Kusang has no doubts.

00:43:06.480 --> 00:43:07.540
Kusang, tell him what it is.

00:43:07.780 --> 00:43:08.100
Yeti!

00:43:08.280 --> 00:43:09.300
Same as you saw before.

00:43:09.560 --> 00:43:09.840
Same.

00:43:10.080 --> 00:43:12.250
That's the expert, Doc.

00:43:12.810 --> 00:43:14.470
Guess maybe you might have made a mistake, huh?

00:43:15.330 --> 00:43:16.010
Let's get it covered.

00:43:16.660 --> 00:43:17.300
Let it go.

00:43:18.050 --> 00:43:18.750
What do you mean, let it go?

00:43:18.750 --> 00:43:20.010
But Delango, a Himalaya monkey,

00:43:20.090 --> 00:43:21.370
you'll find one of the harper zoos in the world.

00:43:21.450 --> 00:43:21.990
Kusang said it!

00:43:22.070 --> 00:43:23.010
Forget about Kusang.

00:43:23.620 --> 00:43:25.520
He's never seen the creature we're looking for.

00:43:26.100 --> 00:43:27.810
Yeti! Yeti!

00:43:27.850 --> 00:43:28.710
Knock it off, will you?

00:43:28.850 --> 00:43:29.350
Kusang, monkey.

00:43:29.430 --> 00:43:29.970
Oh, you're trapping me.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.860
is to practically remain one of our own men.

00:43:32.650 --> 00:43:32.990
Jack?

00:43:33.230 --> 00:43:34.190
Yeah, he just happened to fall into one of our fans.

00:43:34.190 --> 00:43:37.970
No, that's just a flycatch.

00:43:39.500 --> 00:43:40.600
Let's take him over to catch.

00:43:41.360 --> 00:43:42.560
Come on, Jack. Come on like me.

00:43:42.680 --> 00:43:43.280
You'll be all right.

00:43:44.870 --> 00:43:45.230
Dead in.

00:43:45.740 --> 00:43:46.680
Koshang, tie him down.

00:43:47.160 --> 00:43:58.100
What is it?

00:43:59.190 --> 00:43:59.970
Well, apart from the bleeding...

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:02.580
It may be a cracked bone, but that's an X-ray, I can't tell.

00:44:03.140 --> 00:44:03.800
Does that hurt?

00:44:04.660 --> 00:44:06.720
Ed, are you sure you've got the right station on that?

00:44:06.900 --> 00:44:07.500
It should be.

00:44:08.410 --> 00:44:10.510
I'll fix it with him to give us a weather forecast, Doc.

00:44:13.860 --> 00:44:15.070
Guy to come up to us?

00:44:30.510 --> 00:44:31.430
Heavy snow continuing.

00:44:33.500 --> 00:44:36.660
Demons and lizards.

00:44:36.800 --> 00:44:37.540
That's all we need.

00:44:37.800 --> 00:44:39.000
We've got 24 hours.

00:44:39.360 --> 00:44:40.740
Listen, this man can't march tomorrow.

00:44:40.920 --> 00:44:41.500
It's out of the question.

00:44:41.660 --> 00:44:43.080
Well, Tom, we'll dig out the sledge.

00:44:43.310 --> 00:44:44.150
You've got a sledge?

00:44:44.310 --> 00:44:44.490
Yeah.

00:44:44.630 --> 00:44:45.690
Yeah, but it's not for him.

00:44:45.930 --> 00:44:46.590
Well, what's it for, then?

00:44:47.050 --> 00:44:49.190
Listen, Doc, this expedition cost a lot of money.

00:44:49.310 --> 00:44:50.530
I'm not going back empty-handed.

00:44:51.220 --> 00:44:54.000
That animal we got in a cage out there, you say some kind of a monkey.

00:44:54.160 --> 00:44:54.660
Well, of course it is.

00:44:54.680 --> 00:44:56.960
Well, that's the mysterious yeti or snowman.

00:44:57.100 --> 00:44:57.640
We've proved it.

00:44:57.820 --> 00:44:59.000
Kusang here confirms it.

00:44:59.100 --> 00:44:59.300
Meaning?

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.200
Meaning that, from now on, we sell that fact.

00:45:03.060 --> 00:45:06.980
I gotta get that brute down to India, that particular verified specimen of the Yeti.

00:45:07.500 --> 00:45:08.260
Sales promotion.

00:45:08.500 --> 00:45:10.220
I can do it. I know how to handle it.

00:45:10.320 --> 00:45:12.040
Sure, Tom. Like with Franchini, that guy.

00:45:12.040 --> 00:45:12.380
Shut up.

00:45:12.800 --> 00:45:14.380
Franchini case? Were you mixed up in that?

00:45:14.440 --> 00:45:15.520
He doesn't know what he's talking about.

00:45:15.520 --> 00:45:17.960
There's no Tom Friend in it, if I remember. How long have you used that name?

00:45:17.960 --> 00:45:21.080
I used what name I like, is what case do you think you're talking about.

00:45:21.280 --> 00:45:22.540
The Indian wolf children.

00:45:23.080 --> 00:45:24.480
Allegedly reared by wolves in the jungle,

00:45:24.720 --> 00:45:27.200
and then turned out to be plain mental defectives.

00:45:28.000 --> 00:45:29.540
All right, that's what the people wanted.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:31.480
Another new concept for humanity.

00:45:32.460 --> 00:45:34.640
You're nothing but a cheap fairground trickster.

00:45:34.800 --> 00:45:35.820
I don't like your business!

00:45:38.560 --> 00:45:44.830
Taking care of the weather forecast.

00:45:48.270 --> 00:45:51.220
I don't know what makes you lose control.

00:45:52.720 --> 00:45:54.390
I'm sorry, Doc.

00:45:54.860 --> 00:45:55.400
Forget it.

00:45:55.620 --> 00:45:57.570
How do you feel, McNee?

00:46:01.440 --> 00:46:01.900
Make me.

00:46:03.180 --> 00:46:03.900
What's he hearing?

00:46:04.220 --> 00:46:04.920
Hush, listen.

00:46:08.290 --> 00:46:10.080
Cage, torch it.

00:46:11.310 --> 00:46:12.330
Bring some players.

00:46:12.490 --> 00:46:12.570
Yeah.

00:46:15.280 --> 00:46:16.100
Come on, we may need you.

00:46:27.730 --> 00:46:29.280
Cage, it's all twisted.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:31.830
It's gone. It's gone away.

00:46:32.290 --> 00:46:34.970
And the door, it's all reached off.

00:46:35.750 --> 00:46:37.130
I just don't understand this.

00:46:37.840 --> 00:46:40.010
Let's see. Let's see if we can figure out the tracks.

00:46:40.540 --> 00:46:42.380
Oh, the snow's all trampled about.

00:46:43.130 --> 00:46:45.000
Hey, what's this? Look, there's this track.

00:46:45.940 --> 00:46:48.150
Hey, look at that. They're two different kinds.

00:46:48.750 --> 00:46:50.150
Look at the size of it.

00:46:50.950 --> 00:46:52.970
Fifteen, sixteen inches long.

00:46:54.310 --> 00:46:57.310
There's no doubt about it. There was something else here, too.

00:46:57.470 --> 00:46:58.150
Put that torch out.

00:46:58.580 --> 00:46:59.880
Yeah. What are we gonna do? Kind follow?

00:47:01.620 --> 00:47:03.560
Tuzang, get the rifles, quick!

00:47:03.940 --> 00:47:05.920
Check what's happening! Quick, get the rifles!

00:48:00.480 --> 00:48:01.500
There's something by the tent!

00:48:02.640 --> 00:48:03.000
Kursang!

00:48:11.400 --> 00:48:12.100
Frank, what was it?

00:48:12.300 --> 00:48:13.000
Was it you that yelled?

00:48:13.620 --> 00:48:13.980
Kursang!

00:48:14.490 --> 00:48:16.040
Hey, Tom, look!

00:48:16.410 --> 00:48:17.770
Don't be dressed all around here!

00:48:17.970 --> 00:48:18.330
McNeigh?

00:48:22.750 --> 00:48:23.110
McNeigh?

00:48:24.750 --> 00:48:25.470
Are you all right?

00:48:25.630 --> 00:48:26.110
What was it?

00:48:26.380 --> 00:48:26.820
You okay?

00:48:27.000 --> 00:48:27.400
I don't know.

00:48:27.440 --> 00:48:27.840
Give me a gun.

00:48:27.980 --> 00:48:28.580
Some of those prayers.

00:48:29.140 --> 00:48:29.600
Come on!

00:48:35.980 --> 00:48:38.000
What did you see? Coussaint told me.

00:48:38.770 --> 00:48:40.310
I see! I see!

00:48:40.650 --> 00:48:43.240
What man must not see!

00:48:43.680 --> 00:48:44.340
I see!

00:48:44.480 --> 00:48:46.280
Through the acting!

00:48:47.080 --> 00:48:49.280
You made me see!

00:48:50.600 --> 00:48:51.360
Coussaint!

00:49:53.800 --> 00:49:54.300
What's that?

00:49:54.300 --> 00:49:55.680
Your trap's all broken apart.

00:49:58.550 --> 00:49:58.970
Come on.

00:50:08.720 --> 00:50:10.160
Can he sign a coussin?

00:50:10.360 --> 00:50:12.580
No, you can bet he's headed back home by now.

00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:14.900
Going down, it'll only take him a few hours.

00:50:15.120 --> 00:50:16.160
He's nearly out of his mind.

00:50:16.530 --> 00:50:18.870
Yeah, well, he had good cause to me if he saw what did this.

00:50:19.030 --> 00:50:21.150
But with this and those footprints,

00:50:21.270 --> 00:50:23.490
you can get a pretty good idea of the weight of the thing that made him.

00:50:23.910 --> 00:50:24.790
Looks like you were right, Doc.

00:50:25.320 --> 00:50:27.540
Partly. But don't forget the vital part.

00:50:28.080 --> 00:50:29.980
This creature may have an affinity for man, sir.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:31.140
something in common with ourselves.

00:50:31.890 --> 00:50:33.330
Let's remember that before we start shooting.

00:50:33.450 --> 00:50:34.190
Sure, sure.

00:50:35.490 --> 00:50:36.650
Is he getting delirious?

00:50:36.770 --> 00:50:37.590
I'm afraid so.

00:50:38.410 --> 00:50:39.750
You took care of his ankle.

00:50:39.970 --> 00:50:40.750
I did what I could.

00:50:40.850 --> 00:50:42.490
This is in the hospital, and that's where he ought to be.

00:50:42.530 --> 00:50:43.530
Oh, give him another shot of dough.

00:50:43.630 --> 00:50:44.250
No, he's had enough.

00:50:45.050 --> 00:50:46.170
All right, MacNeil, all right.

00:50:46.610 --> 00:50:47.470
Go to sleep, old boy.

00:50:47.690 --> 00:50:48.290
You're fine.

00:50:49.120 --> 00:50:50.120
MacNeil, did you hear what I said?

00:50:53.570 --> 00:50:55.170
He's almost in the condition of trance.

00:50:55.580 --> 00:50:55.900
Trance?

00:50:56.000 --> 00:50:57.660
This is the way I found him after the thing had been here.

00:50:57.860 --> 00:50:58.560
What are you getting at?

00:50:58.640 --> 00:50:59.180
I'm not sure.

00:50:59.740 --> 00:50:59.980
You mean...

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.700
And he's affected by him in some way?

00:51:01.900 --> 00:51:02.680
It's not impossible.

00:51:02.980 --> 00:51:04.700
If he were hypersensitive to their presence...

00:51:04.700 --> 00:51:05.220
Their presence?

00:51:05.970 --> 00:51:07.890
When he gets like this, they might be close?

00:51:08.110 --> 00:51:09.130
It's only a wild guess.

00:51:09.640 --> 00:51:11.790
McNeigh, McNeigh, the eyes.

00:51:14.120 --> 00:51:17.400
McNeigh, he's in a complete state of trance.

00:51:18.750 --> 00:51:19.970
McNeigh, can you understand me?

00:51:20.420 --> 00:51:21.400
Can you hear me, McNeigh?

00:51:23.390 --> 00:51:23.790
Pulse.

00:51:39.020 --> 00:51:41.860
I think there's something out there on the ice.

00:51:42.000 --> 00:51:43.840
I got it, Tom! I got it!

00:52:43.760 --> 00:52:44.220
Be careful, Tom.

00:52:48.030 --> 00:52:48.210
Dead.

00:52:51.220 --> 00:52:51.700
That's it.

00:52:53.140 --> 00:52:53.660
Really it.

00:52:55.400 --> 00:52:56.300
Abominable snowman.

00:52:57.500 --> 00:52:58.480
Ties of that body.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:04.710
Looks like you underestimated, Doc. Must be 10 feet. It'll be 11 feet high.

00:53:04.990 --> 00:53:07.680
Yeah, that face.

00:53:10.640 --> 00:53:11.460
There's more of them.

00:53:12.840 --> 00:53:13.320
They know.

00:53:15.240 --> 00:53:16.780
Listen, we gotta get this thing back to camp.

00:53:17.960 --> 00:53:19.040
We must be able to manage.

00:53:20.010 --> 00:53:21.690
Ed, get a rope and a sledge. Give me your gun.

00:53:22.910 --> 00:53:23.190
Right.

00:54:32.300 --> 00:54:35.760
The porter's come back. The one they took with him, the man named Cusain.

00:54:35.820 --> 00:54:37.980
You must be green. No, I'm not. I saw him in the courtyard.

00:54:38.260 --> 00:54:40.260
He seemed exhausted and could hardly stand up.

00:54:40.620 --> 00:54:42.360
He's not there now. They took him away.

00:54:43.350 --> 00:54:45.690
He was there, Foxy. They took him through that door.

00:54:46.130 --> 00:54:48.510
I've got to know what this means. I'm going to see the llama.

00:54:48.630 --> 00:54:50.390
Helen, you'll never see him at this hour. You'll...

00:55:52.240 --> 00:55:55.720
Drink! You've been frightened.

00:55:56.420 --> 00:55:59.920
One of my servants found you wandering in the secret part of the building.

00:56:00.400 --> 00:56:01.660
I was looking for you.

00:56:02.260 --> 00:56:03.200
Cousin's come back.

00:56:03.740 --> 00:56:04.140
Cousin?

00:56:04.260 --> 00:56:06.220
The porter who went with my husband and the others.

00:56:06.340 --> 00:56:07.520
I saw him in the courtyard.

00:56:07.820 --> 00:56:08.720
You're mistaken.

00:56:09.180 --> 00:56:12.480
No, but I'm not mistaken. I saw him, I tell you, in the courtyard.

00:56:12.660 --> 00:56:14.040
It was not Cousin.

00:56:14.180 --> 00:56:15.520
But I swear to you.

00:56:15.520 --> 00:56:16.780
You are concerned for your husband.

00:56:18.060 --> 00:56:19.660
He's in danger, I'm sure of it.

00:56:20.350 --> 00:56:27.920
Danger? Yes. They are in danger, all of them, from their own actions.

00:56:28.140 --> 00:56:29.980
I don't understand you, but you've got to help me.

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:31.460
Do something, warn them, bring them back.

00:56:31.620 --> 00:56:32.820
I can do nothing.

00:56:33.020 --> 00:56:33.320
Why?

00:56:33.820 --> 00:56:37.600
It is not possible to bend the destiny of men.

00:56:38.100 --> 00:56:43.140
The fate of your husband will be governed by his own nature.

00:56:56.590 --> 00:56:59.900
Mr. Fox, you will conduct this lady.

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:01.760
back to her living quarters.

00:57:02.100 --> 00:57:03.380
I'm so sorry about this, sir.

00:57:03.860 --> 00:57:04.180
Come on.

00:57:05.160 --> 00:57:05.460
Wait.

00:57:05.660 --> 00:57:08.240
Get me away from...

00:57:10.790 --> 00:57:12.830
Don't you realize the hopelessness of it?

00:57:12.970 --> 00:57:14.410
We've got to try and find them, Foxy.

00:57:14.490 --> 00:57:16.230
There's no way of telling where they are by now.

00:57:16.410 --> 00:57:18.090
With three or four native guides, we'll have a chance.

00:57:18.170 --> 00:57:18.790
Native guides?

00:57:18.930 --> 00:57:20.350
I'll tackle those porters down there.

00:57:20.430 --> 00:57:22.850
You'll never persuade them to go, not into those high valleys.

00:57:23.030 --> 00:57:23.370
I think I can.

00:57:23.410 --> 00:57:25.210
But supposing the lama forbids them to?

00:57:25.540 --> 00:57:27.260
Listen, Foxy, they're waiting for money, aren't they?

00:57:27.480 --> 00:57:28.600
Well, I can give it to them.

00:57:31.950 --> 00:57:34.230
For heaven's sake, Helen, you're not going to give them all that.

00:57:34.490 --> 00:57:36.270
I'll give them everything I've got, Foxy.

00:57:36.410 --> 00:57:38.670
All right, well, let me handle it. We don't want to overdo it.

00:57:38.850 --> 00:57:39.770
There's one of them now.

00:57:40.950 --> 00:57:44.200
Where are the others? Where are the others?

00:57:45.300 --> 00:57:47.400
Well, call them for me. Call them.

00:57:47.520 --> 00:57:50.140
Go your pooper, how do you know? Go your pooper, how do you know?

00:57:50.340 --> 00:57:51.500
Go your pooper, how do you know?

00:57:56.410 --> 00:57:59.820
All right. All right, now, I want you both more.

00:58:03.200 --> 00:58:08.520
The herald angels.

00:58:09.050 --> 00:58:10.130
What's the matter now?

00:58:13.630 --> 00:58:14.790
I'll come when I can!

00:58:16.250 --> 00:58:18.400
We're transferred into the cave.

00:58:18.930 --> 00:58:20.530
It'll give us protection against heavy snows.

00:58:20.770 --> 00:58:22.590
Don't tell me friend's delaying here from my side.

00:58:22.630 --> 00:58:25.150
Oh, no. No, he's not satisfied with the bag so far.

00:58:25.870 --> 00:58:27.750
In a couple of days, this foot of yours should be usable.

00:58:28.090 --> 00:58:28.770
Thanks to you.

00:58:30.250 --> 00:58:33.290
Tell me, what does it look like?

00:58:33.560 --> 00:58:34.140
The dead one?

00:58:34.300 --> 00:58:34.640
Uh-huh.

00:58:35.370 --> 00:58:37.130
Well, you'll see, bears out a lot of my guesses.

00:58:37.680 --> 00:58:38.220
It's massive?

00:58:38.560 --> 00:58:40.560
And its height is about ten foot five inches.

00:58:40.940 --> 00:58:42.480
Weight, six hundred and fifty pounds.

00:58:42.600 --> 00:58:44.280
Its age is difficult to assess without...

00:58:44.280 --> 00:58:45.500
No, that's not what I mean.

00:58:46.890 --> 00:58:48.730
Didn't you see what it looked like?

00:58:49.170 --> 00:58:49.750
The face?

00:58:51.020 --> 00:58:51.380
Yes.

00:58:52.380 --> 00:58:53.660
Well, there's nothing ached-like about it.

00:58:54.160 --> 00:58:55.240
There's nothing human, either.

00:58:55.320 --> 00:58:56.970
That I felt it had...

00:58:57.280 --> 00:58:57.960
Go on, go on.

00:58:58.880 --> 00:58:59.980
A sadness and...

00:59:00.600 --> 00:59:03.970
There's probably only a surface resemblance to wisdom.

00:59:07.840 --> 00:59:08.300
How's it feel?

00:59:09.220 --> 00:59:09.440
Better.

00:59:10.170 --> 00:59:12.340
Try and ease that boot on slowly,

00:59:12.870 --> 00:59:14.610
and I'll take these packs down and come back for you.

00:59:18.820 --> 00:59:19.600
There a minute, all right?

00:59:20.150 --> 00:59:21.940
Ah, come around the side.

00:59:23.450 --> 00:59:27.720
See if we can get a few more purges.

00:59:27.960 --> 00:59:28.160
Okay.

00:59:33.710 --> 00:59:45.840
I'll get you down there now.

00:59:46.020 --> 00:59:55.790
It's gone.

00:59:55.990 --> 00:59:56.270
Gone.

00:59:56.450 --> 00:59:57.490
Without this one, I'd go.

01:00:47.370 --> 01:00:48.190
It would be instantaneous.

01:00:51.890 --> 01:00:52.530
They killed him.

01:00:55.700 --> 01:00:56.840
It was the sound of that howling.

01:00:59.080 --> 01:00:59.960
He couldn't stand it.

01:01:00.540 --> 01:01:02.400
He fell because his foot was useless.

01:01:04.290 --> 01:01:05.090
They killed him.

01:01:08.140 --> 01:01:21.760
You all right? What happened?

01:01:22.630 --> 01:01:24.590
I just got to it. The gun, Tom, I just got to it.

01:01:24.630 --> 01:01:25.550
Another second. What happened?

01:01:26.510 --> 01:01:29.960
They came at me. Two of them. You just done a...

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:30.540
I don't know what it's like.

01:01:31.170 --> 01:01:32.050
Closed to in the light.

01:01:32.430 --> 01:01:32.510
There.

01:01:32.690 --> 01:01:32.970
Here.

01:01:33.490 --> 01:01:33.870
Take a drink.

01:01:34.180 --> 01:01:34.940
How did it happen?

01:01:35.340 --> 01:01:36.080
Take it easy, Ed.

01:01:37.270 --> 01:01:37.690
Go on.

01:01:38.260 --> 01:01:40.760
Hey, they just came out of the cave,

01:01:41.580 --> 01:01:43.940
and these two came running towards me.

01:01:45.000 --> 01:01:45.760
The size of them.

01:01:45.920 --> 01:01:47.840
You wouldn't credit the speed that they could move.

01:01:48.420 --> 01:01:49.180
I grabbed my gun.

01:01:49.200 --> 01:01:49.620
Yeah, I know.

01:01:49.760 --> 01:01:51.660
You blasted off enough to start an avalanche,

01:01:51.700 --> 01:01:52.160
but you missed it.

01:01:52.160 --> 01:01:52.960
Yeah, it was like this.

01:01:53.240 --> 01:01:55.120
The sun was in my eyes, and I couldn't get organized.

01:01:56.350 --> 01:01:57.880
Tom, they're after me.

01:01:58.230 --> 01:01:59.610
They know it was me that did it last night.

01:01:59.730 --> 01:01:59.970
They're after me.

01:02:01.120 --> 01:02:02.340
They just killed McNeil.

01:02:02.380 --> 01:02:02.560
What?

01:02:03.340 --> 01:02:03.980
It was an accident.

01:02:04.490 --> 01:02:05.250
It's me next.

01:02:05.450 --> 01:02:06.170
They know it was me.

01:02:07.180 --> 01:02:07.860
Ah, don't worry.

01:02:07.920 --> 01:02:08.820
I've had this before.

01:02:09.500 --> 01:02:12.220
Me and a grizzly once, we ran a war of nerves a whole winter.

01:02:12.380 --> 01:02:13.340
I can handle it.

01:02:13.710 --> 01:02:14.530
But we want to act.

01:02:14.590 --> 01:02:15.810
That's what we want to do right now.

01:02:17.670 --> 01:02:19.370
Hey, Tom, let's get some action.

01:02:19.570 --> 01:02:20.590
Why don't we just sit around?

01:02:20.950 --> 01:02:21.870
We know they're up there.

01:02:21.930 --> 01:02:23.190
Why don't we go up there and find them?

01:02:23.330 --> 01:02:24.370
Look, Ken, I got an idea.

01:02:25.140 --> 01:02:26.240
You've had a lot of tough assignments.

01:02:27.080 --> 01:02:27.820
Can you handle one more?

01:02:28.020 --> 01:02:28.800
Well, that's what I want.

01:02:28.980 --> 01:02:29.560
Yeah, action.

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:31.760
Can you rig that steel net up in the roof of that cave?

01:02:34.350 --> 01:02:35.150
Yeah, I guess so.

01:02:35.330 --> 01:02:36.950
Throw a little trap or anything that might go in there.

01:02:37.070 --> 01:02:37.950
I could do that.

01:02:38.620 --> 01:02:39.600
What about springing the trap?

01:02:39.720 --> 01:02:40.180
Who does that?

01:02:43.360 --> 01:02:43.960
I get it.

01:02:44.980 --> 01:02:45.480
I do.

01:02:46.360 --> 01:02:48.140
I'm in the back there acting as bait, right?

01:02:48.500 --> 01:02:48.780
Right.

01:02:50.540 --> 01:02:52.020
You're a character, Tom.

01:02:52.520 --> 01:02:53.700
Ah, sure, I'll do it.

01:02:53.720 --> 01:02:54.680
I told you that's what I wanted.

01:02:54.800 --> 01:02:56.860
Let's get to work while it's still got me in mind.

01:03:00.350 --> 01:03:02.160
Yeah, let's get it cleared.

01:03:02.470 --> 01:03:03.310
Give me a spade.

01:03:03.840 --> 01:03:04.800
Ah, here's one.

01:03:05.150 --> 01:03:06.170
What do you want a spade for?

01:03:07.600 --> 01:03:08.420
Oh, yeah, jock.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:46.260
Here we must go on.

01:03:46.340 --> 01:03:47.080
We damned, not now.

01:03:47.360 --> 01:03:48.720
Come in, we're going to camp here.

01:03:49.550 --> 01:03:49.950
Jokpoche.

01:03:50.210 --> 01:03:51.490
Listen, it's the slightest encouragement.

01:03:51.670 --> 01:03:52.190
They'll all desert.

01:03:52.470 --> 01:03:54.050
And this time you'll never get them back.

01:03:54.550 --> 01:03:54.950
Jokjeere.

01:03:55.860 --> 01:03:56.920
Kewa de ganga, you.

01:03:59.250 --> 01:03:59.570
Tom!

01:04:00.120 --> 01:04:01.660
It's all fixed. Come and look.

01:04:01.930 --> 01:04:11.020
Right. There she is.

01:04:11.930 --> 01:04:14.230
One pull on this, and the whole thing comes down.

01:04:14.640 --> 01:04:15.380
I'm sure it'll work.

01:04:15.580 --> 01:04:17.890
I've tested and tried. Nice work, eh, Doc?

01:04:18.350 --> 01:04:20.010
You know my feelings. I don't like the idea.

01:04:20.150 --> 01:04:21.170
You're part in it least of all.

01:04:21.900 --> 01:04:23.160
If you want my advice...

01:04:23.160 --> 01:04:24.560
Listen, Doc, he doesn't need your advice.

01:04:24.990 --> 01:04:26.450
He can pull out any time he wants to.

01:04:26.450 --> 01:04:27.270
Who wants to pull out?

01:04:27.310 --> 01:04:28.830
It's all business, of course, but I should have thought

01:04:28.830 --> 01:04:29.710
where the risk can't be calculated.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:32.520
Anything falls, anything underneath, it'll be fully occupied.

01:04:32.860 --> 01:04:36.120
That's tungsten steel with a breaking strain of 20,000 pounds.

01:04:36.700 --> 01:04:38.920
More struggles, the more the whole thing tightens on it.

01:04:39.440 --> 01:04:42.350
In addition to which, there you are, Ed, clean and loaded.

01:04:42.570 --> 01:04:44.670
Thanks, Tom. Just in case I should need it.

01:04:44.750 --> 01:04:45.450
Just in case.

01:04:45.770 --> 01:04:47.010
Ah, you can trust me.

01:04:47.540 --> 01:04:50.360
I am trusting you with this unique specimen when it shows up.

01:04:52.520 --> 01:04:54.080
It's beginning to snow out there again.

01:04:55.550 --> 01:04:58.160
Listen, Ed, we'll keep you covered from the tent.

01:04:58.380 --> 01:04:59.700
Check every half hour, but...

01:05:00.220 --> 01:05:01.540
Oh, when anything happens, you signal.

01:05:02.050 --> 01:05:03.110
You bet I'll signal.

01:05:03.310 --> 01:05:03.530
Right.

01:05:07.370 --> 01:05:09.430
This is complete madness, friend, and you know it.

01:05:10.040 --> 01:05:10.820
Relax, will you?

01:05:11.080 --> 01:05:12.580
He knows how to hold his fire.

01:06:01.310 --> 01:06:02.990
You can't see the cave.

01:06:03.230 --> 01:06:03.990
Yeah, so far.

01:06:04.350 --> 01:06:05.430
You better call it off.

01:06:06.240 --> 01:06:06.820
Call it off?

01:06:07.340 --> 01:06:09.220
This snow may be just the thing they're waiting for.

01:06:09.400 --> 01:06:10.780
That man's depending on you.

01:06:10.780 --> 01:06:12.400
If he gets in trouble, I'm gonna help him.

01:06:12.540 --> 01:06:12.900
Don't worry.

01:06:13.120 --> 01:06:13.380
Fiend.

01:06:14.280 --> 01:06:15.680
Why not settle for the bomb we've got?

01:06:15.990 --> 01:06:16.930
I've said no.

01:06:17.110 --> 01:06:17.990
You've cracked the mystery.

01:06:18.150 --> 01:06:19.150
You've proved the creature exists.

01:06:19.350 --> 01:06:19.870
Settle for that.

01:06:20.010 --> 01:06:20.810
Take back a dead one?

01:06:20.890 --> 01:06:21.370
If we can.

01:06:21.690 --> 01:06:21.990
Uh-uh.

01:06:22.150 --> 01:06:24.500
Have him pickle it and write out learned reports,

01:06:24.620 --> 01:06:27.220
stick a skeleton in a museum and call it something other rather solid.

01:06:27.300 --> 01:06:28.340
I'm not looking for credit.

01:06:28.780 --> 01:06:29.900
No, not gonna be like that.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:30.500
He's mine.

01:06:30.620 --> 01:06:31.720
Like the famous wolf children?

01:06:32.340 --> 01:06:33.280
Just the opposite.

01:06:33.480 --> 01:06:34.280
This is no fake.

01:06:34.480 --> 01:06:35.800
That's why I'm not going to give up.

01:06:36.430 --> 01:06:38.710
I'm going to prove to him I can bring back the real thing.

01:06:38.850 --> 01:06:41.050
You can't drag this down to a personal level.

01:06:41.170 --> 01:06:41.950
It's far too important.

01:06:42.150 --> 01:06:42.830
Not to me.

01:06:44.240 --> 01:06:46.220
Listen, there's a warning.

01:06:46.910 --> 01:06:50.150
It's strong, intelligent, may have powers we haven't even developed.

01:06:50.650 --> 01:06:51.910
It might have inherited the Earth.

01:06:52.660 --> 01:06:53.260
Something went wrong.

01:06:53.980 --> 01:06:57.060
And here it is, the last vestige of a species hiding away where nothing else will live,

01:06:57.820 --> 01:06:59.920
waiting in misery and despair for final extinction.

01:07:00.960 --> 01:07:02.420
I don't have to point the morrow.

01:07:02.840 --> 01:07:06.960
Look, if they drop the H-bomb, your descendants too may wind up in the ice.

01:07:28.440 --> 01:07:28.880
See anything?

01:07:30.440 --> 01:07:38.200
I thought, no, let's, let's have a cigarette.

01:08:14.560 --> 01:08:15.700
See a thing around us.

01:08:30.120 --> 01:08:30.860
Wrecked to pieces.

01:08:35.440 --> 01:08:40.700
He's dead.

01:08:41.700 --> 01:08:41.860
Dead?

01:08:42.840 --> 01:08:45.310
Robert, how did they kill him?

01:08:45.430 --> 01:08:46.450
I can't find any mark.

01:08:47.030 --> 01:08:48.010
It looks like a heart attack.

01:08:49.200 --> 01:08:49.480
Face.

01:08:49.660 --> 01:08:50.760
I think he died from shock.

01:08:52.760 --> 01:08:53.560
He didn't lose the gun.

01:08:53.720 --> 01:08:53.960
Why?

01:08:54.260 --> 01:08:59.460
The magazine's empty.

01:09:04.280 --> 01:09:07.720
It's strange. Each shell's been struck by the firing of him. They didn't go off.

01:09:08.610 --> 01:09:13.130
They didn't go off, friend. You loaded the gun. What with? Dummy ammunition?

01:09:13.410 --> 01:09:23.320
I didn't want another dead one. I knew he'd fire even after Nat held. He was scared.

01:09:24.950 --> 01:09:28.210
Where did they beat at this? Your gun must have frightened them off.

01:09:28.330 --> 01:09:29.740
I think this was all they wanted.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:30.800
You mean they weren't after Ed?

01:09:30.920 --> 01:09:31.100
No.

01:09:31.260 --> 01:09:31.980
Oh, but they killed him?

01:09:32.200 --> 01:09:33.300
No, they didn't, friends.

01:09:36.900 --> 01:09:37.360
You did.

01:10:34.320 --> 01:10:41.730
Think that'll stop them?

01:10:43.000 --> 01:10:45.720
They'll give us a fighting chance if they decide to attack.

01:10:46.290 --> 01:10:46.970
If they do.

01:10:47.440 --> 01:10:48.480
You think they won't, huh?

01:10:49.520 --> 01:10:50.280
Let me tell you something.

01:10:51.360 --> 01:10:53.180
I'm not going to take any chances on losing that one.

01:10:54.100 --> 01:10:54.480
No, sir.

01:10:55.360 --> 01:10:57.600
We'll do like you said, Doc, be satisfied with the one we got.

01:10:58.620 --> 01:10:59.480
Decision's a little late.

01:11:01.330 --> 01:11:02.270
It's cold in here.

01:11:03.050 --> 01:11:03.810
Want a drink, Doc?

01:11:04.900 --> 01:11:05.720
No, no thanks.

01:11:06.150 --> 01:11:08.740
Yeah, we gotta keep alert, keep our circulation up.

01:11:08.800 --> 01:11:09.420
Be ready for him.

01:11:09.980 --> 01:11:12.220
Get a hit the first time, there may not be a second chance.

01:11:14.820 --> 01:11:18.390
It's on your mind.

01:11:19.010 --> 01:11:20.010
I wonder what they'll try.

01:11:20.150 --> 01:11:20.370
Try?

01:11:20.610 --> 01:11:22.170
They know you've got a gun and what it can do.

01:11:22.190 --> 01:11:23.050
They knew Ed had a gun.

01:11:23.130 --> 01:11:23.830
That didn't stop him.

01:11:23.910 --> 01:11:25.590
Well, they knew, oh, you knew about Sherry's gun.

01:11:26.040 --> 01:11:28.860
You mean they could swat transfer us?

01:11:29.680 --> 01:11:29.980
I don't.

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:30.400
Don't give me that.

01:11:32.220 --> 01:11:33.420
Let's get something straight, Doc.

01:11:34.450 --> 01:11:36.810
These are animals, dangerous killers.

01:11:37.210 --> 01:11:38.420
And that's all they are.

01:11:38.750 --> 01:11:40.290
MacKee died from an accident.

01:11:40.940 --> 01:11:42.400
Shelly died of his own fear.

01:11:43.470 --> 01:11:44.870
It isn't what's out there that's dangerous,

01:11:45.810 --> 01:11:46.930
but it's what's in us.

01:11:47.280 --> 01:11:48.280
What are you doing there?

01:11:48.820 --> 01:11:53.480
I'm wondering, wondering how old that face is.

01:11:54.410 --> 01:11:55.450
It's seen a long life.

01:11:56.350 --> 01:11:57.610
Longer than ours, I should say.

01:11:57.790 --> 01:11:59.810
A hundred years, perhaps more.

01:12:01.470 --> 01:12:03.690
Now, this isn't the face of a savage thing.

01:12:03.970 --> 01:12:05.360
There's gentleness.

01:12:05.460 --> 01:12:05.840
Gentleness?

01:12:06.020 --> 01:12:09.460
Suppose they're not just a pitiable remnant waiting to die out.

01:12:10.140 --> 01:12:13.450
Now, waiting, yes, was waiting for us to go.

01:12:13.650 --> 01:12:15.030
For mankind to die out?

01:12:16.890 --> 01:12:19.710
It was something the Lama said about taking thought

01:12:19.710 --> 01:12:20.810
for man's successors.

01:12:21.580 --> 01:12:24.530
I didn't understand then, but suppose we're the savages?

01:12:24.730 --> 01:12:25.230
We're what?

01:12:25.600 --> 01:12:27.120
Are you out of your mind, Doc?

01:12:27.630 --> 01:12:29.550
Perhaps for them, we've been the Dark Ages.

01:12:30.510 --> 01:12:31.670
We've flattered ourselves too long.

01:12:32.300 --> 01:12:34.920
Perhaps we're not homo sapiens, thinking man,

01:12:35.690 --> 01:12:37.050
what has our thinking brought us to,

01:12:37.800 --> 01:12:40.860
but homo vastans, man the destroyer.

01:12:42.710 --> 01:12:44.390
When the world knows about these creatures,

01:12:45.160 --> 01:12:46.180
they're destroyed too.

01:12:47.370 --> 01:12:48.190
Of course we're men.

01:12:48.880 --> 01:12:50.880
We can only be here to destroy them.

01:12:51.640 --> 01:12:52.860
They must be aware of that.

01:12:53.020 --> 01:12:54.360
You mean, we're the enemy, huh?

01:12:54.700 --> 01:12:56.960
If they can deal with us, the secret's kept.

01:12:57.780 --> 01:12:59.100
It's their only chance of survival.

01:12:59.290 --> 01:12:59.970
Up here on the ice?

01:13:00.150 --> 01:13:05.360
survival for what it's enough until perhaps their time comes talk you better

01:13:05.360 --> 01:13:09.810
have a drink we better have something to eat yeah it's a good idea then we'll

01:13:09.810 --> 01:13:13.400
take turns on watch throw me something to one of those self-heating cans will you

01:13:13.400 --> 01:13:17.000
like living inside of an iceberg here one soup coming up

01:13:41.100 --> 01:13:41.340
Fred?

01:13:42.160 --> 01:13:42.520
Yeah?

01:13:43.290 --> 01:13:43.890
Where's the radio?

01:13:44.110 --> 01:13:45.000
Over there.

01:13:45.530 --> 01:13:46.490
It's all smashed up.

01:13:46.670 --> 01:13:47.030
Smashed?

01:13:47.170 --> 01:13:50.110
If you're thinking of trying to fix it, you can forget it.

01:13:50.250 --> 01:13:50.670
It's had it.

01:13:50.890 --> 01:13:51.590
But didn't you hear?

01:13:52.260 --> 01:13:52.700
Hear what?

01:13:52.860 --> 01:13:55.390
I told you that thing is wrecked.

01:14:01.920 --> 01:14:03.620
Friends, we must get out of here.

01:14:04.250 --> 01:14:05.330
What's the matter with you?

01:14:05.870 --> 01:14:08.230
We're going to get out of here when it's daylight and not before.

01:14:08.550 --> 01:14:09.770
What's the matter with you? You cracking up?

01:14:11.330 --> 01:14:13.950
Maybe that's it. Talk to altitude sickness.

01:14:14.730 --> 01:14:17.460
Yeah, well, go get some oxygen. Right over there.

01:14:18.560 --> 01:14:20.720
Go ahead, just turn the tap. It's all ready for use.

01:14:21.200 --> 01:14:21.560
Adios.

01:14:21.800 --> 01:14:24.370
I want you going sick on me.

01:14:26.780 --> 01:14:28.380
Won't be easy managing that sludge tomorrow.

01:14:28.640 --> 01:14:29.980
All that new snow bound to...

01:14:30.060 --> 01:14:38.000
Make it unstable. Feeling better?

01:14:42.670 --> 01:14:46.580
It'll be tough going. We'll just have to get out in the middle of the glass here and just keep going.

01:14:46.700 --> 01:14:47.560
That's all. Keep going.

01:15:00.380 --> 01:15:00.680
Ed.

01:15:00.820 --> 01:15:18.320
How are you? Did you hear that?

01:15:18.460 --> 01:15:22.530
What can you hear?

01:15:27.140 --> 01:15:28.320
I can hear him yelling out there.

01:15:28.940 --> 01:15:29.480
They caught him!

01:15:31.700 --> 01:15:33.000
Ed! Ed, I can hear you!

01:15:33.360 --> 01:15:35.840
You've got to understand, that isn't Shelley, it isn't anybody!

01:15:35.960 --> 01:15:36.780
I can hear his voice!

01:15:36.840 --> 01:15:39.180
It's in your own mind! It's just happened to me too!

01:15:39.480 --> 01:15:40.340
I've got to send him!

01:15:40.420 --> 01:15:41.560
Listen, Shelley's dead!

01:15:41.800 --> 01:15:43.180
No, no, that's a mistake!

01:15:43.380 --> 01:15:44.580
Ed, you've got to understand!

01:16:04.570 --> 01:16:28.490
Wait a minute, we're gone!

01:16:36.520 --> 01:16:45.590
See ya!

01:18:00.410 --> 01:18:00.590
Oh.

01:18:30.860 --> 01:18:31.120
Three!

01:21:33.290 --> 01:21:33.690
I feel it.

01:21:53.080 --> 01:21:54.100
My knees follow me.

01:21:54.200 --> 01:21:54.860
Come on, hold up.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:32.780
This has been for you a severe trial.

01:23:33.040 --> 01:23:36.970
All your companions died in all these accidents.

01:23:37.290 --> 01:23:43.480
And with all the sufferings, you did not find what you went out to seek.

01:23:45.000 --> 01:23:58.070
I was wrong. Wrong? What I was looking for does not exist. You are certain of that? Yes. There is snow.

01:24:00.220 --> 01:24:00.360
and
